  "body": "## What changed\n\nU12 of #3663: the Holders page of the tool library window gets a search and a header row, and a user holder opens in an editable holder form.\n\n**List (screen 4)**\n- One header row: the search box, the count \"N of M holders\", **New holder…**, **Import…** and **Export…**.\n- The search matches the taper, the clamp, a bore or collet size and the name. Each term must match (\"BT40 ER32\", \"shrink 12\"). A number also matches a holder that clamps a shank of that size (\"er 16\" shows the ER chucks that take Ø16). Esc in the box clears it.\n- The search result is kept for its input (`state_holder_search.rs`). A still frame searches nothing.\n- The read-only note and the empty \"USER HOLDERS\" text are removed from the list. The user holders section shows when the document has a user holder.\n- **New holder…** copies the ER32 chuck of the machine taper (else BT40 ER32) as a user holder (one undo step) and opens it in the form.\n- **Import…** and **Export…** are disabled. Their hover text names #4389.\n\n**Holder form (screen 5)**\n- Inputs: Name, Spindle taper, Clamp (ER11 to ER50, Weldon side lock, shrink fit), Clamps from / to, Gauge length, Largest diameter, Nose diameter (mm).\n- The drawing to scale has the spindle nose box above the gauge line and the shank range below the nose. The drawing keeps room for its labels, so no label is cut off (`holder_drawing.rs`, shared with the read-only view).\n- \"Used by N tools\" lists the tools whose component stack uses the holder. A click opens the tool.\n- Footer: Duplicate, Cancel, Apply. The hint says \"Apply updates N tools. It is one undo step.\"\n- Apply is one undoable `EditDocumentComponent`. It derives each tool that uses the holder again in the same undo step. An edit that breaks the fit of a tool is refused by name, and nothing changes.\n- A value that cannot describe steel is refused by name before Apply. Apply is then disabled with the reason, and the reason shows under the fields.\n- A built-in holder opens read-only, with \"Copy as user holder\", as before.\n- **Edit outline…** and **Import model (STEP)…** are disabled. Their hover text names #4390.\n\n**Outline safety (crates/tools)**\n- New `holder_library::HolderShape` (`holder_library_shape.rs`). The form's values build the outline with the holder library's own `HolderEntry::points`. Thus the law \"never smaller than the steel\" holds for the stated values: the ER nut over its full length, the Weldon body plus `WELDON_SCREW`, the shrink nose and body plus `SHRINK_MARGIN`, the flange as a full cylinder.\n- `HolderShape::of` reads the shape back from a component. It accepts the shape only when the outline that the shape makes is the outline of the component. A holder with another outline (a DXF profile) opens in the generic component editor, as before.\n- No project-file change: the shape comes from the machine side, the workpiece side and the outline.\n\nUI choices: `docs/decisions/4338-holders-page.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/tools` (`holder_library::shape::tests`):\n- `each_builtin_taper_holder_reads_back_as_its_shape`\n- `an_edited_outline_is_never_smaller_than_the_steel` (samples the outline of a grid of edited shapes against the stated steel, and the flange)\n- `a_value_that_cannot_be_steel_is_refused_by_name`\n- `an_outline_from_elsewhere_is_not_a_form_shape`\n\n`crates/ui` (`egui_app::tests::tool_library_holder_form`):\n- `the_holder_search_matches_each_term_and_counts` (AND terms, a number in a clamp range, \"N of M holders\", Esc clears)\n- `a_still_frame_searches_reads_and_checks_nothing` (counter tests for the search, the shape read, the check and the drawing; a changed input runs each again)\n- `each_holder_field_lands_in_one_step_with_its_tools_and_undoes` (name, taper, gauge length, largest diameter, nose diameter: one undo step, both tools derive again, undo gives both back)\n- `the_clamp_and_the_shank_range_land_and_undo` (New holder, clamp ER32 to Weldon, Clamps from / to sets the bore)\n- `an_edit_that_breaks_a_tools_fit_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_built_in_holder_is_read_only_and_copies_and_duplicates`\n\nLayout: `layout_window_holders` (updated: the header row) and `layout_window_holder_form` (new). Updated: `each_face_has_its_hint`, `a_built_in_holder_copies_as_a_user_holder_and_its_gauge_is_edited` (the copy opens in the form now).\n\n`crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 1964 before, 1971 after.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll results are on head `82b8eca37` (lane mac-1, pool). This head merges `main` (the #1120 tool inks): the holder drawing uses the theme inks (`tool_axis`, `tool_body`, `tool_edge`, `tool_dim`, `tool_note`, `tool_ground`), so it adds no colour literal.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 22 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (tools lib, app build, app `machine_default_holder` and `mcp_holder`, ui build, ui lib, 16 ui suites incl. `theme_files`). Log `gate-4338-82b8eca37.log`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed (release build, motion light lib, adaptive_troch island / neck / parallel, app pocket_pass_start). Log `gate-4402-82b8eca37-light.log`.\n- The pinning tests above run in the tools lib step and the ui lib step.\n- No post and no toolpath change: the example catalog suites do not apply. No heavy step (P6).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Import / Export of holder files (#4389), Edit outline and STEP import (#4390): the buttons are disabled.\n- MCP: the shape edit has no MCP tool yet: `MCP: edit a user holder by its shape fields` #4391. MCP can replace the row with `upsert_tool_component` today.\n- Inch input on the form: the form edits in mm.\n- The holder rail at the left of the mockup's form is not drawn. \"‹ List\" goes back to the searchable list.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (main): the list has a bare filter box and no actions; a holder opens read-only, with a clipped drawing.\n\n![before list](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/before-list.png)\n![before holder](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/before-holder.png)\n\nAfter: the list with its header row and count.\n\n![after list](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/after-list.png)\n\nAfter: the search \"bt40 er 16\" (each term must match; 16 is in the clamp range).\n\n![after search](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/after-search.png)\n\nAfter: a new user holder in the holder form, with the spindle nose box and the shank range.\n\n![after form](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/after-form.png)\n\nAfter: a nose diameter that cannot surround the collet range is refused by name; Apply is disabled.\n\n![after form refusal](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/after-form-refusal.png)\n\nAfter: a built-in holder stays read-only with \"Copy as user holder\".\n\n![after builtin view](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4402/after-builtin-view.png)\n\nChangelog: Tool library: the Holders page searches the taper, the clamp, a size and the name, and a user holder opens in an editable form (taper, clamp, clamping range, gauge length, diameters) with a drawing of the spindle nose and the shank range; Apply updates each tool that uses the holder in one undo step, and refuses an edit that breaks a tool's fit.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4338\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
